{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,26]],"date-time":"2026-10-26T16:36:56Z","timestamp":1793032616782,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"ASME International","issue":"2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[1955,6,1]],"date-time":"1955-06-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":-460339200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.asme.org\/publications-submissions\/publishing-information\/legal-policies"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["asmedigitalcollection.asme.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":[],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1955,6,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>A symbolic notation devised by Reuleaux to describe mechanisms did not recognize the necessary number of variables needed for complete description. A reconsideration of the problem leads to a symbolic notation which permits the complete description of the kinematic properties of all lower-pair mechanisms by means of equations. The symbolic notation also yields a method for studying lower-pair mechanisms by means of matrix algebra; two examples of application to space mechanisms are given.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1115\/1.4011045","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,6,4]],"date-time":"2021-06-04T15:24:04Z","timestamp":1622820244000},"page":"215-221","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1115\/crossmarkpolicy-asme","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":3398,"title":["A Kinematic Notation for Lower-Pair Mechanisms Based on Matrices"],"prefix":"10.1115","volume":"22","author":[{"given":"J.","family":"Denavit","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"The Technological Institute, Northwestern University, Evanston, Ill."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"R. S.","family":"Hartenberg","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"The Technological Institute, Northwestern University, Ev